Large responses recognize title labels, issue-record markup, initial definite
articles and code declarations. Small negative values mark personal pronouns,
auxiliaries, and short word pieces joined to a preceding word. URL
hostname openings and dot leaders have small positive responses. These rules
capture broad patterns, not the component's many individual word preferences.
