"""Startup token shape, followed by a small first-person-intention response.

At the start of a document (also while its first token simply repeats),
attached code/path fragments have large positive values; tabs, backticks,
and opening curly quotation marks have negative values. The constants are
coarse averages of these readable token families, not token-ID lookups.
Inside ordinary text, respond negatively to 'let me/us', 'let's', and
first-person future constructions. Most other positions are near zero.
