"""A pulse on the initial run of a document, scaled by token spelling.

An uninterrupted repetition of the initial token is still treated as an
onset. The pulse is stronger for ordinary words than for digits, punctuation
or line endings. These are coarse token-class averages, not word-specific
values. After different text arrives, only a tiny background remains.
