Short capital-letter pieces get positive values, especially after another
capital. English word frequency suppresses familiar words; the preceding
fragment's capital count suppresses long capitalized runs. Short, moderately
uncommon lower-case clusters get a smaller response. Everything else is near
zero, apart from coarse document-start priors and a few formatting patterns.
These are fitted group averages, not exact lexical or contextual predictions.
