"""layers.1.mlp.down_proj:5740 - a lexical detector for a few word pieces.

Fires on whole words and word fragments, not on meaning:
  * positive on the words "lift", "lifting", "lifted", "lifts", "luck", "truck", "trucks"
    (and "ift" split off right after an "l", as in "l|ift");
  * negative on the sound "lum" when it stands alone as a piece (" lum", "olum", "plum",
    "ulum", "llum", "imum", "lumen") - as in electro|lum|inescent, vell|um, Petal|uma;
  * negative on "um"-type pieces that come right after a piece ending in "l"
    (vell|um, McColl|um, Antebell|um, Bl|um, electrol|um);
  * a large positive on the Japanese character 吊 (to hang or suspend).
Everything else predicts 0. It reads only the current token and the token before it,
within the same document.
